# Tests are acceptance

Every behavior change ships with a test that states the accepted behavior. A change without that test is not done.

- Name acceptance tests `TestAcceptance_<Behavior>`.
- Put the cases in a table when the behavior is a list of situations (Go wiki: TableDrivenTests).
- Test use cases through their public inputs and outputs. Drive adapters with a temporary directory or a temporary SQLite file, not a fake of the thing under test.
- A port fake is allowed only at the boundary the use case does not own (OS folder dialog, OS trash UI).
- When a prompt lists acceptance tests, those tests are the definition of done. Add the missing case before declaring the prompt finished.
- Update the doc that describes the behavior in the same change as the test.

```go
func TestAcceptance_ExactGroupRecommendsPlainName(t *testing.T) {
    got := Recommend(group)
    if got.Keeper != "a.jpg" {
        t.Fatalf("keeper = %s", got.Keeper)
    }
}
```
